{%- comment -%}
  APEX product card.

  Accepts:
  - card_product: {Object} Product (required)
  - lazy_load:    {Boolean} lazy-load the image. Default true.
  - cta_label:    {String} button label. Default "Shop now".

  Replaces Dawn's `card-product` on the collection grid only. Dawn's card is
  built for a light `card_color_scheme` surface and carries vendor, rating,
  quick-add, volume-pricing and swatch machinery this catalogue does not use;
  none of it could be styled onto the dark ground without fighting six
  stylesheets at once.

  MEDIA. Uses `featured_image`, like a standard Shopify collection — the image
  a merchant sets on the product is the image the collection shows, and it
  stays in step with search, related products and every other surface.

  It previously preferred `custom.pack_image` (the transparent PNG the
  homepage pack grid uses) on the grounds that the shop's featured images are
  shot on white and punch a white rectangle into this dark band. That is still
  true, and it is now a MERCHANDISING problem rather than a theme one: the fix
  is a featured image that suits the ground, not a card that quietly shows a
  different picture than the one the merchant chose.

  PRICE PER UNIT is the real decision axis for a consumable sold in five pack
  sizes, and the pack grid does not show it anywhere. Derived from
  `custom.pack_label` (the same metafield driving the homepage numerals) via
  `times: 1`, which yields 0 for a blank or non-numeric value — hence the
  `> 1` guard, which also suppresses a pointless "$9.99 / pack" on a 1-pack.

  ONE TAB STOP. The whole card is a single <a>; the CTA is a styled <span>
  inside it, not a nested link. A visible button that is not separately
  focusable is the correct trade here — duplicating the destination would put
  two identical tab stops on every card, which is worse for keyboard use than
  one.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign lazy_attr = 'lazy'
  if lazy_load == false
    assign lazy_attr = 'eager'
  endif
  assign label = cta_label | default: 'Shop now'
  assign alt_text = card_product.title | escape

  assign media = card_product.featured_image

  assign pack_count = card_product.metafields.custom.pack_label.value | times: 1
  assign show_unit_price = false
  if pack_count > 1 and card_product.price > 0
    assign unit_price = card_product.price | divided_by: pack_count
    if unit_price > 0
      assign show_unit_price = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

<article class="apex-pcard{% unless card_product.available %} apex-pcard--soldout{% endunless %}">
  <a class="apex-pcard__link" href="{{ card_product.url }}">
    <div class="apex-pcard__media">
      {%- if media != blank -%}
        {{
          media
          | image_url: width: 800
          | image_tag:
            loading: lazy_attr,
            class: 'apex-pcard__img',
            alt: alt_text,
            widths: '200,300,400,600,800',
            sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 280px, (min-width: 750px) 30vw, 42vw'
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="apex-pcard__placeholder" aria-hidden="true">
          {{ 'product-apparel-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'apex-pcard__placeholder-svg' }}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- unless card_product.available -%}
        <span class="apex-pcard__badge">{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}</span>
      {%- endunless -%}
    </div>

    <div class="apex-pcard__body">
      <h3 class="apex-pcard__title">{{ card_product.title | escape }}</h3>

      <p class="apex-pcard__price">
        <span class="apex-pcard__amount">
          {%- if card_product.price_varies -%}
            {{ 'products.product.price.from_price_html' | t: price: card_product.price_min | money }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ card_product.price | money }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>

        {%- if card_product.compare_at_price > card_product.price -%}
          <s class="apex-pcard__was">{{ card_product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>

      {%- if show_unit_price -%}
        <p class="apex-pcard__unit">{{ unit_price | money }} / ball</p>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Keeps the CTA on a common baseline across a row when one product is
          missing its pack_label. An empty <p> would be announced as nothing,
          but aria-hidden makes that explicit rather than incidental.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="apex-pcard__unit apex-pcard__unit--empty" aria-hidden="true"></p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <span class="btn btn-outline apex-pcard__cta">{{ label }}</span>
  </a>
</article>
